; Correctly rounded division by a constant: the divisor's significand, its
; rounded reciprocal and the exponent factor are constants (no rcp, no Newton
; step, no NaN test of the divisor), and for a divisor of moderate size the
; factor is applied first with no test of the dividend's size. A huge
; divisor keeps the test.

